  "nl_text": "The schemabench_0120 database is a collection of tables that store information about a fictional basketball league. The database includes tables for regular season results, detailed results, seasons, teams, tourney seeds, tourney slots, and target.\nThe regular season results table contains information about the results of games played during the regular season, including the season, day number, winning team, losing team, winning score, losing score, location of the game, number of overtime periods, and whether the game was a tie. The table also includes primary keys for season, day number, winning team, and losing team.\nThe detailed results table contains information about the results of games played during the regular season, including the season, day number, winning team, losing team, winning score, losing score, location of the game, number of overtime periods, and various statistics for each team, such as field goals made and attempted, free throws made and attempted, rebounds, assists, steals, and blocks. The table also includes primary keys for season, day number, winning team, and losing team.\nThe seasons table contains information about each season, including the season number, day zero, region W, region X, region Y, and region Z. The table also includes a primary key for season number.\nThe teams table contains information about each team, including the team ID and team name. The table also includes a primary key for team ID.\nThe tourney seeds table contains information about the seeds for each team in the tournament, including the season, seed, and team. The table also includes primary keys for season and seed.\nThe tourney slots table contains information about the slots for each team in the tournament, including the season, slot, strong seed, and weak seed. The table also includes primary keys for season and slot.\nThe target table contains information about the predicted results of games, including the ID, season, team ID 1, team ID 2, predicted result, team ID 1 wins, and team ID 2 wins. The table also includes primary keys for ID and season.\nOverall, the schemabench_0120 database is a comprehensive collection of tables that provide detailed information about a fictional basketball league, including regular season results, detailed results, seasons, teams, tourney seeds, tourney slots, and target.",
  "gold_question": "Background / Context\n\nThe project is to develop a data-driven application for analyzing the 2015 NCAA Basketball Tournament. The system will manage and analyze tournament data, including regular season and tournament results, team performance metrics, seeds, and slots. The existing database schema supports the storage and retrieval of historical match data and predictive modeling information.\n\nObjectives\n\nThe main objective is to provide users with a comprehensive platform for accessing and analyzing NCAA tournament data. The system should enable detailed performance analysis and prediction of match outcomes based on historical data.\n\nStakeholders & Users\n\n- Sports Analysts: To analyze tournament data and derive insights.\n- Coaches and Team Managers: To understand team performance and opponent analysis.\n- Data Scientists: For predictive analytics and modeling match outcomes.\n- Basketball Enthusiasts: For accessing tournament data and statistics.\n\nFunctional Descriptions\n\n1. Data Management: \n   - Store and retrieve regular season and tournament data, including detailed match statistics such as scores, location, and number of overtimes.\n   - Manage team information and season data, including regions, seeds, and slots.\n\n2. Performance Analysis:\n   - Provide detailed statistical analysis of regular season and tournament matches.\n   - Allow comparison of team performance metrics and historical outcomes.\n\n3. Predictive Modeling:\n   - Enable prediction of match outcomes using historical data and predefined models.\n   - Store prediction results and evaluate prediction accuracy.\n\n4. User Interface:\n   - Develop an intuitive interface for data visualization and analysis.\n   - Provide tools for filtering and querying team and match data easily.\n\nNon-Functional Descriptions\n\n- Performance: The system should efficiently handle large datasets and ensure quick query responses.\n- Scalability: Support scalability to accommodate future expansion of data and users.\n- Security: Ensure secure access to sensitive data and analytics features.\n- Reliability: Maintain high availability and reliability of data analysis and prediction services.\n- Usability: Prioritize user-friendly design for diverse user groups, including non-technical users.",
  "input_json": "/data/SchemaBench/Experiment/schema2text_codellama13b/0120.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: schemabench_0120\nCREATE TABLE `regular_season_results` (\n  `season` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `day_number` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `winning_team` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `losing_team` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `winning_score` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `losing_score` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `location` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `overtime_periods` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `is_tie` tinyint(1) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`season`, `day_number`, `winning_team`, `losing_team`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `detailed_results` (\n  `season` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `day_number` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `winning_team` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `losing_team` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `winning_score` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `losing_score` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `location` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `overtime_periods` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `field_goals_made` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `field_goals_attempted` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `free_throws_made` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `free_throws_attempted` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `rebounds` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `assists` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `steals` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `blocks` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`season`, `day_number`, `winning_team`, `losing_team`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `seasons` (\n  `season_number` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `day_zero` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `region_w` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `region_x` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `region_y` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `region_z` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`season_number`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `teams` (\n  `team_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `team_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`team_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `tourney_seeds` (\n  `season` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `seed` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `team` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`season`, `seed`),\n  CONSTRAINT `tourney_seeds_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`season`) REFERENCES `seasons` (`season_number`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `tourney_seeds_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`team`) REFERENCES `teams` (`team_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `tourney_slots` (\n  `season` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `slot` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `strong_seed` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `weak_seed` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`season`, `slot`),\n  CONSTRAINT `tourney_slots_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`season`) REFERENCES `seasons` (`season_number`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `target` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `season` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `team_id_1` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `team_id_2` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `predicted_result` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `team_id_1_wins` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `team_id_2_wins` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`, `season`),\n  CONSTRAINT `target_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`season`) REFERENCES `seasons` (`season_number`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `target_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`team_id_1`) REFERENCES `teams` (`team_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `target_ibfk_3` FOREIGN KEY (`team_id_2`) REFERENCES `teams` (`team_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
